    {
      "type": "multiple-choice",
      "id": 2,
      "difficulty": "Easy",
      "prompt": "$\\int \\cos^2 x\\,dx$ uses which identity?\nA) $\\cos^2 x=1-\\sin^2 x$ only\nB) $\\cos^2 x=\\frac{1+\\cos 2x}{2}$\nC) $\\cos^2 x=\\frac{1-\\cos 2x}{2}$\nD) none",
      "answer": "B) $\\cos^2 x=\\frac{1+\\cos 2x}{2}$",
      "solution": {
        "steps": [
          "Half-angle for even powers. Key is B."
