      "difficulty": "Medium",
      "prompt": "For $\\int\\frac{dx}{\\sqrt{9-x^2}}$, substitute:\nA) $x=3\\tan\\theta$\nB) $x=3\\sin\\theta$\nC) $x=3\\sec\\theta$\nD) $x=9\\sin\\theta$",
